 "final_passage": "Across the five-dataset suite at horizon 96, Halyard achieved lower test MAE than Tidewell on four datasets (Kelso-Grid: 0.231 vs 0.247; Marrick-Traffic: 0.284 vs 0.301; Ashby-Retail: 0.517 vs 0.538; Pell-Solar: 0.176 vs 0.189) and matched Tidewell on Doveton-Weather (0.412 vs 0.412). Halyard also outperformed seasonal-naive on all five datasets, with lower test MAE in every case (e.g., Kelso-Grid: 0.231 vs 0.312; Pell-Solar: 0.176 vs 0.244). However, because no statistical tests were reported and the advantage over Tidewell was not uniform (a tie on Doveton-Weather), the evidence does not establish that Halyard reliably outperforms Tidewell across the suite.",
